# Invoria Web — project conventions

This rule summarizes how **invoria-web** is built. For full detail, follow the linked `ai/` and `docs/` files (single source of truth — do not duplicate them in PRs).

## Stack

- **Angular 21** — standalone components (do not set `standalone: true`; default in v20+), signals, `rxResource`, lazy routes, native control flow (`@if`, `@for`)
- **PrimeNG 21** + **@primeuix/themes** (`AuraInvoria` preset in `src/styles/primeng/aura.preset.ts`) — interactive UI
- **Tailwind CSS v4** — layout/spacing/semantic utilities from `src/styles/tokens.css` + `@theme` in `src/styles.css`
- **RxJS 7.8** — services return `Observable`; pages use `toSignal` / `rxResource` / `linkedSignal`
- **Vitest** — `ng test`; specs as `*.spec.ts`
- **Prettier** — 100 cols, single quotes (`.prettierrc`)
- **TypeScript strict** — `strictTemplates`, no implicit returns
- API base: `environment.apiUrl` (prod via `API_URL` — see `README.md`)

## App layout (`src/app/`)

| Area | Role |
|------|------|
| `features/<name>/` | Domain: `pages/` (smart), `components/` (dumb), `services/*-api.service.ts`, `models/` |
| `layout/` | `DashboardShell`, navbar, sidebar |
| `core/` | `ApiResponse`, `Paging`, `Entity`, HTTP interceptors, error presenters |
| `shared/` | `ui/` (`EmptyState`, `SurfaceCard`, `PageHeader`), `requests/` (e.g. `PagingQueryRequest`) |

**Selector prefix:** `app`. **Routing:** lazy `loadChildren` / `loadComponent` in `app.routes.ts` under dashboard shell.

## Feature rules

- **Smart pages** (`pages/`): `inject()` services, router, route; URL/query state; `rxResource` + optional `linkedSignal` for lists; scoped `MessageService` + `p-toast`.
- **Presentational** (`components/`): `input()` / `output()` / `model()` only — **no** `*-api.service` or router.
- **Services:** `providedIn: 'root'`, `HttpClient`, `Observable<ApiResponse<T>>`, `environment.apiUrl`.
- **Models:** `*.entity.ts` (extends `Entity`), `*-*.request.ts` for HTTP bodies/queries; **no** feature-level barrel re-exports in `models/`.
- **Cross-feature imports:** forbidden except documented exceptions — see [ai/ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ai/ARCHITECTURE.md) §7 (orders↔customers/products, customers↔orders, products↔inventory, suppliers↔procurement).

**Reference implementation:** Customers — [ai/component-design-rules.md](../../ai/component-design-rules.md), `src/app/features/customers/`.

## UI & styling

- **PrimeNG first** for interactive controls (`p-table`, `p-dialog`, `p-button`, `p-paginator`, `p-toast`, `p-tag`, etc.).
- **Tailwind** for layout, spacing, typography; use semantic classes (`bg-surface`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, `text-danger`) — not raw hex.
- **Avoid** large `styles: []` / component CSS unless PrimeNG + Tailwind cannot express it (document why).
- **Dark mode:** `.dark` on `html` or `body`; PrimeNG uses `darkModeSelector: '.dark'`.
- **Forms:** Reactive Forms + PrimeNG controls for non-trivial flows.

## List pages

- Query params: `page` (1-based), `pageSize` (default **25**, options `[25, 50, 100, 200]` unless feature documents otherwise).
- Filters on **pages** (debounced ~700ms); list components stay dumb and emit `pageChange` / `clearFilters`.
- Row actions: match **View** / **View Details** pattern in `order-list` — see [docs/frontend-list-conventions.md](../../docs/frontend-list-conventions.md).
- Products list spacing/filters: [.cursor/rules/products-list-layout.mdc](./products-list-layout.mdc).

## Angular practices

- `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` where used; `class` bindings (not `ngClass`); signals `update`/`set` (not `mutate`).
- Import order: Angular → RxJS → PrimeNG → app (`core`, `shared`, feature).
- Use `presentApiError` / `ApiResponse` handling from `core/http`; request literals with `satisfies` where appropriate.

## Testing

- **Vitest** via `ng test`; mock API services in page specs; stub PrimeNG/jsdom needs (e.g. `ResizeObserver` for Tabs).
- **Orders** layer mapping: [.cursor/rules/orders-testing-architecture.mdc](./orders-testing-architecture.mdc)
- Orders only: `npx ng test --watch=false --include="src/app/features/orders/**/*.spec.ts"`

